The '''Karuulm Slayer Dungeon''' is a dungeon located beneath [[Mount Karuulm]], which is located just west of [[Lovakengj]]. It contains a variety of monsters, most notably [[Hydra|hydras]] which cannot be found anywhere else. Upon entering the dungeon, players will encounter a chamber with the [[Tasakaal]], the masters of the [[Kahlith]] just above; they will not converse with players until [[The Ascent of Arceuus]] [[quest]]. This chamber also contains a [[mysterious pipe]] shortcut requiring 88 [[Agility]] which leads players outside the Alchemical Hydra's chambers.

As the dungeon is found inside a volcano, players who wish to explore further beyond the entrance chamber must wear the [[boots of stone]], [[boots of brimstone]] or [[granite boots]] to protect themselves from the [[extreme heat]] of the dungeon floor. If players attempt to explore further without one of these boots, then they will be warned of the consequences; if players proceed regardless, they will be rapidly burnt, taking 4 damage every tick, which can quickly kill the player. Players who have obtained the rewards from the Elite [[Kourend & Kebos Diary]] will no longer need to wear these boots and can bring other footwear or walk barefoot without taking damage.

Throughout the dungeon, players can find opened [[Stone chest (Karuulm Slayer Dungeon)|stone chests]] which can be searched for some [[old notes (Karuulm Slayer Dungeon)|old notes]]. These are written by a [[Dragonkin]] named [[Karuulm]], and documents the various projects he's worked on in creating the draconic inhabitants of the dungeon. Players can compile all the old notes into the [[Mount Karuulm diary]], which documents Karuulm's notes in a chronological order.

The dungeon itself is single-way combat. A [[dwarf multicannon]] can be used in all areas here except the [[wyrm]] and [[Alchemical Hydra]] areas; the former states that the electricity the wyrms discharge would render the cannon useless (however, does not stop the cannon from working on the wyrms in [[Wyrmscraig Cavern]]), and the latter states that it would destroy the chemical containers.
[[File:Karuulm Slayer Dungeon entrance.png|thumb|left|The entrance to the slayer dungeon.]]
{{clear|left}}

==Transportation==
*Players can get there via the [[fairy ring]] {{Fairycode|CIR}}. The mountain is a short walk north of this fairy ring.
*The [[skills necklace]] (The [[Farming Guild]]) will take you just south-west of Mount Karuulm.
*The [[Battlefront Teleport]] will take you just south-east of Mount Karuulm.
*Players may use [[Rada's blessing 3]] or higher, which is unlocked after completing the [[Kourend & Kebos Diary|Kourend & Kebos Hard Diary]], to teleport straight to the dungeon using "Mount Karuulm" option. Rada's blessing 3 offers three daily teleports, while Rada's blessing 4 provides unlimited teleports.

